      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Providers like Project:Camp offer emergency education and care to families in Washington state as climate change brings more destructive weather</p><p>One week after evacuating from the wildfires that devastated parts of this eastern Washington city, Mareesha Backman handed over her youngest son to a stranger and took her first deep breath of relief.</p><p>Spokane public schools was hosting what has become a growing part of disaster response: a day camp for children of survivors. Backman showed up that first day feeling “stunned”, she said: hot, poorly showered and underslept. Thanks to the camp’s volunteers, she was able to go to a doctor’s appointment, run errands and simply sit in the air-conditioned quiet of a friend’s home.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/02/project-camp-spokane-wildfire-recovery\">Continue reading...</a>"
